    {
      "target_argument_id": "arg_7e8132c0",
      "ground": "Article 121 of Geneva Convention III imposes a procedural duty to investigate deaths, not a substantive duty of care whose breach constitutes a war crime.",
      "reasoning": "Article 121 requires the Detaining Power to conduct an official enquiry into deaths. It does not create a substantive obligation to prevent all deaths or impose criminal liability for the failure to investigate per se. The commander's liability arises from the underlying act of wilful killing or command responsibility, not from the procedural omission of failing to launch an enquiry under Article 121.",
      "severity": "material",
