      "claim": "The removal of the prisoners from the protected hospital without due warning violated the protection afforded to civilian hospitals under Geneva Convention IV, article 19.",
      "reasoning": "Article 19 of Geneva Convention IV provides that the protection of a civilian hospital may cease only after a due warning has been given and remains unheeded. The prisoners were taken from the ICRC‑protected hospital without any such warning, thereby breaching the treaty protection of the facility.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "type": "treaty",
          "instrument": "gc_iv",
          "article": "19",
          "quoted_text": "The protection to which civilian hospitals are entitled shall not cease unless they are used to commit, outside their humanitarian duties, acts harmful to the enemy. Protection may, however, cease only after due warning has been given, naming, in all appropriate cases, a reasonable time limit, and after such warning has remained unheeded."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The commander failed to fulfill the procedural duty under Geneva Convention III, article 121, to conduct an immediate official enquiry into the deaths of prisoners of war, constituting a breach of treaty obligations.",
      "reasoning": "Article 121 obliges the Detaining Power to launch an official enquiry whenever a prisoner of war dies or is seriously injured. By ordering the withdrawal of the JNA military police and allowing the prisoners to fall into the hands of hostile forces, the commander precluded any such enquiry, violating this procedural requirement.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "type": "treaty",
          "instrument": "gc_iii",
          "article": "121",
          "quoted_text": "Every death or serious injury of a prisoner of war caused or suspected to have been caused by a sentry, another prisoner of war, or any other person, as well as any death the cause of which is unknown, shall be immediately followed by an official enquiry by the Detaining Power."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
